# AI Rendering Architecture Rules

## Purpose

We support two AI response pipelines:

1.  Legacy JSON Mode (stable production path)
2.  Real-Time Streaming Mode (block grammar protocol)

The system must maintain backward compatibility while enabling
progressive UI rendering.

Feature flag: `realTimeStreamingEnabled: Bool`

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Global Non-Negotiable Rules

1.  Legacy flow MUST remain 100% untouched.
2.  Streaming flow MUST NOT reuse legacy parsing logic.
3.  No cross-contamination between pipelines.
4.  Feature flag must be evaluated exactly once per request.
5.  After renderer selection, no further flag branching is allowed.
6.  Streaming mode must NEVER render raw JSON.
7.  Streaming mode must NEVER use JSONDecoder for live parsing.
8.  Legacy mode MUST continue using JSONDecoder.
9.  Context object must never be rendered in UI (both modes).
10. Streaming protocol must be treated as a fixed deterministic grammar.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 2. Feature Flag Rules

The flag controls: - System prompt selection - Model selection - Parser
selection - Renderer selection - Streaming vs non-streaming network mode

It must NOT: - Be checked inside UI views - Be checked inside section
rendering - Be scattered across files

Evaluate once at orchestration level.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 3. Prompt Isolation Rules

Maintain two prompts: - coreSystemRules (Legacy JSON contract) -
coreSystemRules2 (Streaming Block Grammar)

Prompt selection must be isolated in a single provider.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 4. Model Selection Rules

Models must be explicitly mapped per mode. Do not reuse models
implicitly across modes.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 5. Streaming Protocol Rules

Streaming grammar:

\<
```{=html}
<TITLE>
```
> \<
> ```{=html}
> </TITLE>
> ```

\<\<SECTION:type=short_answer\>\> \<
```{=html}
</SECTION>
```

\<\<SECTION:type=details\>\> \<
```{=html}
</SECTION>
```

\<\<SECTION:type=code language=go\>\> \<
```{=html}
</SECTION>
```

\<`<CONTEXT>`{=html}\> \<`</CONTEXT>`{=html}\>

Rules: - Tags must be uppercase. - Tags must be closed properly. - Code
blocks contain raw unescaped code. - Indentation must be preserved. -
Newlines must be preserved. - No JSON allowed. - No markdown allowed. -
No triple backticks. - No escaped newline sequences like `\n`{=tex}. -
CONTEXT must always appear last.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 6. Streaming Parser Rules

Use deterministic state machine.

Allowed states: - idle - readingTitle - readingSectionHeader -
readingSectionContent - readingContext

Requirements: - Append content immediately while
readingSectionContent. - Finalize section only when closing tag
detected. - Parse context silently. - Support graceful fallback. -
JSONDecoder forbidden during live streaming.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 7. Code Rendering Rules

When detecting:

\<\<SECTION:type=code language=xyz\>\>

System must: - Switch UI to code mode immediately. - Use language for
syntax highlighting. - Preserve whitespace exactly. - Never trim leading
spaces. - Never normalize indentation. - Never collapse blank lines.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 8. Legacy Mode Rules

If streaming flag is false: - Use coreSystemRules - Use JSON schema -
Use JSONDecoder - Render after full response received

Legacy files must not be modified.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 9. Separation of Responsibilities

Prompt Layer → Defines grammar\
Model Provider → Selects model\
Renderer → Handles chunks\
Parser → Interprets grammar\
UI → Displays sections\
Storage → Optional transformation for persistence

No layer may overlap responsibility.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 10. Fallback Safety Rule

If invalid grammar detected: - Abort streaming renderer - Log error -
Retry using legacy pipeline

Streaming must never crash UI.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 11. Telemetry Requirements

Log: - Grammar violations - Unclosed blocks - Tag mismatches -
Unexpected EOF - Parser state transitions (debug mode)

